  "question": {
    "text": "A simple pendulum is being used to determine the value of gravitational acceleration <math><mi>g</mi></math> at a certain place. The length of the pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25.0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and a stopwatch with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> resolution measures the time taken for <math><mn>40</mn></math> oscillations to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The accuracy in&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5.40</mn><mi>%</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3.40</mn><mi>%</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4.40</mn><mi>%</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2.40</mn><mi>%</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Time period of the simple pendulum,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>l</mi></mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><mn>25.0</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4.4</mn><mi>%</mi></math></p>"
